WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.049
When she announced that she was

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.699
running for president in January

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.619
2019, Kamala Harris was met with

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.449
glowing profiles, grassroots

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.249
excitement and ready donors.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.019
And she is one of the top tier

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:10.769
candidates.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.149
Yes, she was a prosecutor, yes,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.439
she's a senator, but she's also

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.269
someone who understands what people

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.139
are going through across the

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:16.769
country.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.939
I think there's a good chance that

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.347
you are going to win the nomination.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:21.929
Almost immediately, her campaign was
plagued

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.849
by inconsistent policy positions and

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.439
internal disarray.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.329
Meanwhile, Harris was haunted by

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.679
her tough on crime past as a

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.149
California prosecutor.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.039
You actually blocked evidence.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.539
From being revealed that would have

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.639
freed them until you were forced

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.229
to do so. There is no excuse for

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.089
that. And the people who suffered

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.979
under your reign as prosecutor

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.990
owe you owe them an apology.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.049
This is gonna to sound immodest, but

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.819
I'm obviously a top-tier candidate.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.649
And so I did expect that I would

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.939
be on the stage and take hits

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.019
tonight because there are a lot of

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.099
people that are trying to make the

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.139
stage for the next debate.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.309
For a lot of them, it's do or die.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.419
Well, yeah, and especially when

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.519
people are at zero or 1% or whatever

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.329
she might be at.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.859
Because of her own dismal polling

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.839
numbers. Harris left the race 11

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.639
months later, but Biden picked her

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.499
as his running mate anyway, and

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.969
so she became the first female vice

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.409
president, a black and Asian woman

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.849
with a sleek image and a willingness

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.169
to say things young progressives

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.159
like to hear.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.169
Black lives have not been taken

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.059
seriously as being

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.619
fully human.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.689
We have for generations now

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.389
been defunding public schools,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.429
but yet militarizing police

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.479
departments.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.919
She went on to bungle interviews,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.449
flip-flop repeatedly, and fail to

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.879
own any issue or commit to anything.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.589
Which is to say Harris's vice

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.999
presidency has looked a lot like her

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.589
shambolic presidential campaign.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.119
Now she's considered the Democratic

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.120
frontrunner-in-waiting.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.899
Yet no one can quite explain why.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.099
Talking about the significance of

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.059
the passage of time.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.549
Right. The significance of the

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.319
passage of time.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.149
So when you think about it, there is

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.949
great significance to the passage of

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.088
time.

00:01:54.089 --> 00:01:55.079
"Harris arrives somewhere with the

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.560
plane and the motorcade and the

00:01:56.561 --> 00:01:58.199
Secret Service agents, makes a few

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.119
mostly bland statements, then tells

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.229
whomever she's meeting with about

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.069
how she's going to bring their

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.869
stories back to Washington.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:04.979
Then she's quickly out of sight

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.169
again," wrote Edward-Isaac Dovere

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.247
in The Atlantic in May 2021.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:11.099
Two months prior, Biden had put

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.329
Harris in charge of "leading the

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.919
administration's diplomatic efforts

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.299
to address the root causes of

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.919
migration from El Salvador,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.479
Guatemala and Honduras," as the

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.469
White House put it.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.089
"It was a stopping the seas from

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.769
rising kind of job," says Cato

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.629
Institute immigration analyst

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.859
David J. Bier, especially since

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.389
Harris had no authority to actually

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.639
change U.S. immigration policy.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.169
Still, a vice president could at

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.149
least play a robust rhetorical role

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.039
here, shifting the conversation

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.869
around the issue or rallying

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.279
Democrats behind an inspiring

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.119
message.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.589
But rather than outline a coherent

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.509
policy vision, Harris made a series

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.039
of awkward decisions in the comments

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.479
that angered many Democrats and gave

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.039
fodder to Republicans.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.119
We've been to the border.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.120
You haven't been to the border.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.199
And I haven't been to Europe.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.119
And I mean I don't, I don't.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.859
Harris, whose mom was born in India

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.689
and whose dad is from Jamaica, did

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.699
eventually visit Guatemala, but then

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.169
issued a disappointing statement for

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.699
anyone hoping for a departure from

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.589
Trump's immigration policies.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.509
I want to be clear to

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.979
folks in this region who are

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.899
thinking about making that

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.969
dangerous trek

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.009
to the United States–Mexico border.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.270
Do not come.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.529
Do not come.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.269
If Harris runs for president, she

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.349
can't point to her record as a

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.879
prosecutor because it's mostly

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.929
become an embarrassment.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.325
A San Francisco district attorney,

00:03:26.326 --> 00:03:28.349
she increased prosecutions

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.209
and convictions for misdemeanor

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.069
quality-of-life crimes and pushed

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.689
for giving fewer people access to

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.369
the city's drug court, which offers

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.989
alternatives to incarceration.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.399
She opposed the prostitution

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.349
decriminalization measure, helped

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:41.639
federal officials raid immigrant

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.589
businesses, had misconduct

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.599
by a drug-lab technician, and helped

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.309
launch an anti-truancy initiative

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.599
that would bring criminal charges

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.099
against parents if their kids missed

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.209
too much school.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.399
As California attorney general,

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.839
she fought against the court ruling

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.159
that the state's death penalty was

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.049
unconstitutional, fought to

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.849
keep people in overcrowded prisons

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.949
after a court ordered them released,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.419
defended the state's corrections

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.039
department's denial of surgery for

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.869
transgender inmates and

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.579
refused to back a measure requiring

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.469
more scrutiny in police use-of-force

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.429
cases.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.139
She also fought to shut down the sex

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.339
worker friendly ad platform

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.018
Backpage, while publicly ignoring

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:17.789
sexual misconduct involving Oakland

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.439
Police and an underage girl.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.449
1,974

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.949
people were sent to state prisons

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.239
for possession of marijuana or

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.409
hashish while Harris was

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.969
California's top cop.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.869
First of all, let me just make the

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.679
statement very clear.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.059
I believe we need to legalize

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.060
marijuana.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.509
Part of a politician's job is

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.979
finding a way to work together with

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.419
those in their coalition.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.979
Harris, meanwhile, has struggled to

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.359
work comfortably with even her own

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.189
staff, many of whom departed

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.989
after brief stints on the job.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.699
A June report in Politico described

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.589
Harris's office as tense

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.509
and at times dower marked

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.549
by chaotic moments, low morale

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.869
and low trust.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.639
One person with direct knowledge of

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.469
how Harris's office is run

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.939
described it as an unhealthy and

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.159
abusive environment where people

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.479
are thrown under the bus from the

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.619
very top.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.969
Should Biden run again?

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:04.589
The question is dividing Democrats

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.479
by a September 2022 headline

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.369
in Time about the oldest president

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.929
in U.S. history.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.909
But if not Biden, then who?

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.619
A Los Angeles Times analysis of

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.299
national opinion polls said that as

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.819
of October 2022, 53%

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.589
found Harris unfavorable, a drop of

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.749
14% since she took office.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.339
It's hard to avoid the sense that

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.169
the Democrats have been so enamored

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.489
with the package this particular

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.869
candidate comes in that they're

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.489
willing to overlook what lies

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.989
beneath the surface.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:33.089
Harris's problems are her own, but

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.739
in making her an avatar of its

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.599
future, the party has made her

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.669
problems their own, too, embracing

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.619
box, checking at the expense

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.209
of political or administrative

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.079
competence.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.209
Some say third time's the charm.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.249
But a relative addage here may be,

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.379
Fool me once, shame on you.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.149
Fool me twice, shame on me.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.889
Eventually, Joe Biden will leave

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.209
politics.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.949
When that happens, will Harris fool

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.149
progressives a third time?

